D2DX 0.99.529: keep the resolution the player chose in the game's video options.

D2DX loads its built-in SGD2FreeRes and writes SGD2FreeRes's config
(d2dx_sgd2freeres.json, next to the game) anew at every start, always with
"Ingame Resolution Mode" : 2, the custom size D2DX computes. SGD2FreeRes takes the
resolution chosen in Options > Video Options > Resolution from that file and
writes a new choice back into it, not into the registry. So a choice of 640x480
or 800x600 was lost at the next start.

The app reads the mode of the last game from that file before it starts the game
again. If it is 0 (640x480) or 1 (800x600), the app changes one byte in its own
copy of glide3x.dll in the game's start folder, so that D2DX writes that mode
instead of 2. This happens at run time on the device (class D2IngameResolution);
the glide3x.dll files in the app stay as they are. The change is checked like
the others in tools/binpatch.py: only these three files, the bytes around the
place, and the hash of the result.

  file      glide3x.dll
  before    sha256 c4edd7b6d2b64373ff6f2f8b7d04437a41b14e57b582d7542f09ec1407ae6f89
  after     sha256 a03a2484f7b97044c8f7fcb73465f1b02139c41b14812a16c1df2ef0ec935eb5  (640x480)
  after     sha256 a816d35a5dc3f98606efd72011f4bd6389422c2cfc641461452b9ec0895af634  (800x600)

  file      glide3x-atlas512.dll
  before    sha256 53eab88060db53a34cbff59ee2a223828c862058b590e5167a48369fa631a1e6
  after     sha256 1d38ecdfe97a5d3f534484f554b6af30ac4122fcb17276bb4d8d1bdb7f1e85cb  (640x480)
  after     sha256 20f9b939fb992942c857294b47f5456e25b949f32e8488dbaa75733cd416e647  (800x600)

  file      glide3x-atlas1024.dll
  before    sha256 50e9a58706c2f9f87cafb975e8698d1928725f9f774a78fb954a5d683c5aa313
  after     sha256 a519137a405b80df352b67bce7cf1c823d104581beddf7b5df744df89b4052ba  (640x480)
  after     sha256 c58e07f1757105e0a83440d05e0f779d1ef9497be6dcef6ab6c2215d73edc2c4  (800x600)

  check     file offset 0x3f78d: "Ingame Resolution Mode" : 2,
  change    file offset 0x3f7a8: 32 -> 30 (640x480)
  change    file offset 0x3f7a8: 32 -> 31 (800x600)

The source change it corresponds to (with 0 or 1 for the mode):

--- a/src/d2dx/BuiltinResMod.cpp
+++ b/src/d2dx/BuiltinResMod.cpp
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@
         "           \"800x600\",\r\n"
         "           \"%ix%i\"\r\n"
         "       ],\r\n"
-        "       \"Ingame Resolution Mode\" : 2,\r\n"
+        "       \"Ingame Resolution Mode\" : 0,\r\n"
         "       \"Main Menu Resolution\" : \"800x600\",\r\n"
         "       \"Custom MPQ File\": \"d2dx_sgd2freeres.mpq\",\r\n"
         "       \"Enable Screen Border Frame?\" : true,\r\n"
